{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0198jMEjyUrqNC9QEYVAUJZB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for the \"median\" tier across all planned experiments in the experiment plan. I need to carefully consider the median tier definition and produce realistic predicted results with rationales for each experiment.\n\nLet me analyze the median tier definition:\n- N=16 rho_sj small improvement or flat (0.38-0.43)\n- Cross-dataset: one replicates well (SJ > FK ≥5pp), another weak (delta < 5pp or rho_sj < 0.30)\n- Adaptive compute gain exists but modest (1-3pp)\n- RE conditional analysis direction correct but rho not high, boundary condition needs caveats\n\n\n- Oracle headroom suggests room for improvement but not dramatic\n\nNow I'm looking at the specific metric ranges I need to work within for each experiment. The NER performance on SciERC should stay in that 0.38-0.43 band, cross-dataset replication will be mixed with one strong transfer and one weaker one, adaptive compute gains will be modest, and the relation extraction conditional analysis will show directional correctness without strong correlations. 16_scierc**\n- N=16 on SciERC. Current N=8 rho_sj = 0.3825 (pilot_004). Median: slight improvement to ~0.40-0.41.\n- Oracle headroom with N=16 should be higher than N=8's 0.1085, maybe 0.10-0.12 range.\n- Actually wait, headroom at N=16 should be >= N=8 since more samples means better oracle. But the range says 0.08-0.13. Let me think... N=8 headroom was 0.1085 on pilot_004. N=16 should have higher oracle F1, so headroom should increase. Maybe 0.10-0.13.\n\n**exp-002: ner_conll2003**\n- Cross-dataset comparison. CoNLL-2003 is cleaner and more standardized with just 4 entity types compared to SciERC's 6, so it might be the stronger performer. OntoNotes with 18 types is messier and more complex, likely the weaker cross-dataset result. The simpler annotation scheme in CoNLL could mean tighter distributions and different variance patterns for the sampling-based metrics.\n\n**exp-003: ner_ontonotes**\n- 18 entity types make this the more challenging cross-dataset case. Higher granularity might reduce how well SJ discriminates between samples.\n\n**exp-004: re_diagnostic_analysis**\n- Running a CPU-only breakdown by relation type on the existing data to see if patterns emerge in the median tier.\n\n**exp-005: temperature_sensitivity_analysis**\n- Comparing T=0.7 versus T=1.0 using the pilot data I already have, though I need to double-check which model versions were used in each pilot run.\n\nLooking at the pilot results, the NER scores are nearly identical across temperature settings, suggesting the effect is real but quite small in the median tier.\n\n**exp-006: adaptive_compute_demo**\n- Building on exp-001 to show modest F1 improvements of 1-3 percentage points over the greedy baseline.\n\n**exp-007: ner_multi_model**\n- Testing LLaMA-3.1-8B on SciERC to see if the effect holds with a different model, though likely weaker.\n\n**exp-008: re_n16_confirmation**\n- Increasing N to 16 for RE to get stronger statistical power and confirm the low rho_sj finding.\n\n**exp-009: capability_stratification**\n- Stratifying by difficulty level to reveal the pattern, though boundaries may be less clear-cut.\n\n**exp-010: selection_curves**\n- Plotting best-of-N curves to visualize the SJ advantage, which appears modest overall.\n\n**exp-011: ner_ood_robustness**\n- Testing out-of-distribution robustness to see if performance degrades in the median tier.\n\nNow I'm working through the specific predictions for exp-001, starting with the baseline metrics from pilot_004 and projecting what N=16 should yield—expecting rho_sj around 0.41 with corresponding increases in oracle F1.\n\nFor exp-002, I'm treating this as the stronger cross-dataset case since CoNLL2003 has cleaner annotations and fewer entity types, so I'd expect greedy F1 closer to 0.72, rho_sj around 0.37, and a meaningful gap between SJ and FK correlations.\n\nFor exp-003, OntoNotes is the problematic one with 18 entity types creating more noise—greedy F1 probably drops to 0.58, rho_sj sits around 0.29, and the SJ-FK gap narrows to just 3 percentage points with rho_fk near 0.26.\n\nFor exp-004, I'm looking at relation-type breakdowns where some relations show decent SJ correlation while others don't, and I need to focus on the high-frequency types.\n\nFor exp-005, the temperature sensitivity analysis shows T=0.7 improving signal quality at the cost of diversity—NER sees slightly higher conditional rho with lower oracle headroom, while RE gets more all-zero instances but better conditional rho overall.\n\nFor exp-006, the adaptive compute demo compares SJ-based selection against FK, random, and greedy baselines, with SJ best-of-16 reaching 0.687 (greedy + 2pp), FK at 0.677 (greedy + 1pp), and random at 0.672 (greedy + 0.5pp).\n\nMoving to exp-007, I'm looking at LLaMA-3.1-8B on SciERC—a different model family where greedy F1 might land around 0.60 and rho_sj around 0.35, with SJ still outperforming FK but with a smaller effect size.\n\nFor exp-008, the RE N=16 confirmation shows full rho_sj remaining weak at roughly 0.26 (a slight bump from N=8's 0.244) while conditional rho_sj sits around 0.33, reinforcing the negative finding.\n\nIn exp-009, I'm seeing capability stratification where high-capability instances yield high rho and low-capability instances yield low rho, with a clear boundary emerging between them.\n\nFor exp-010, the selection curves across N=1,2,4,8,16 show SJ consistently above FK, though the gap stays modest throughout.\n\nIn exp-011, out-of-distribution robustness shows rho degrading somewhat, with rho_sj dropping to around 0.30.\n\nNow I'm working through the YAML format with precise numbers, making sure everything stays consistent with the median tier definition and reconciling the values across experiments. Starting with exp-001, I'm setting greedy_f1 at 0.6671 (deterministic for the same model and dataset), oracle_f1_n16 around 0.79, headroom at 0.123, rho_sj_full_n16 at 0.41, and working through the remaining metrics.\n\nFor exp-002, I'm treating this as the \"good\" cross-dataset case with CoNLL being easier at 4 types—greedy_f1 of 0.72, oracle_f1 of 0.82, headroom of 0.10, and a solid SJ-minus-FK gap of 0.07 or more.\n\nFor exp-003 with OntoNotes and its 18 types, the task gets harder, so I'm setting greedy_f1 lower at 0.58 and working through the oracle performance.\n\nNow I'm looking at the metrics for what appears to be the weaker dataset—oracle_f1 around 0.68, headroom still at 0.10, but the SJ-minus-FK gap drops to just 0.03, which falls below the 5 percentage point threshold. The rho_sj value sits right at the boundary around 0.29. I'm reconsidering the tier boundaries based on the median values, where the weaker dataset should have rho_sj between 0.25 and 0.36 and a delta between 0.02 and 0.08, so I'm calibrating the CoNLL case as the stronger one with rho_sj at 0.37.\n\nFor the exp-001 rationale, I'm thinking through why increasing N from 8 to 16 samples only bumps the SJ metric from 0.38 to 0.41—the gain is real and shows tighter confidence intervals, but it's modest because the real constraint isn't sample size but the model's inherent stochasticity at temperature 0.7, where diversity is already quite limited.\n\nFor exp-002, CoNLL-2003's simpler four-type schema (PER, LOC, ORG, MISC) produces cleaner soft Jaccard signals since entity boundaries are less ambiguous and type confusion is minimal. The model gets a higher baseline F1, and the correlation persists because variance comes from genuinely uncertain cases like nested or boundary-ambiguous entities. Soft Jaccard shows a clear 7-point advantage over Fleiss' Kappa because it captures partial entity overlaps that Kappa misses entirely.\n\nFor exp-003, OntoNotes' eighteen fine-grained types introduce substantial type confusion that inflates soft Jaccard scores without necessarily reflecting true accuracy improvements—when the model swaps \"GPE\" for \"LOC\" across samples, soft Jaccard still registers high similarity since both are location-related types.\n\nNow I'm working through the experimental results for the relation extraction tasks and temperature sensitivity analysis.\n\nFor the temperature sensitivity work, I'm checking the pilot data—pilot_004 at T=1.0 shows rho_sj around 0.38, while pilot_005 at T=0.7 is still running. The tradeoff between temperature settings is fairly tight: lower temperature gives slightly better conditional correlation but reduces oracle headroom, though the difference is modest enough that either could work for the median tier prediction. I need to be careful. The plan description says pilot_004 is T=1.0 and pilot_005 is T=0.7. But pilot_004 used ft_002_v2. Let me just predict for the analysis.\n\nNER at T=1.0 (pilot_004): rho_sj=0.3825, headroom=0.1085\nNER at T=0.7 (pilot_005): rho_sj maybe ~0.39, headroom maybe ~0.095\nRE at T=1.0 (pilot_004): full rho_sj=0.2441, cond rho_sj=0.3161\nRE at T=0.7 (pilot_005): full rho_sj maybe ~0.23, cond rho_sj maybe ~0.34\n\nLooking at the temperature effects, lower T boosts conditional signal quality but hurts diversity in the oracle headroom, and for RE tasks it increases all-zero predictions while improving signal on the conditional instances. For exp-006, the adaptive compute demo with N=16 shows SJ achieving 0.6871 F1 (a 2.0pp gain over greedy), which outperforms both FK and random sampling, though still well below the 0.79 oracle ceiling. In exp-007, the fine-tuned LLaMA model on SciERC reaches around 0.60 greedy F1. (slightly worse than Qwen3-8B)\n- rho_sj: ~0.35\n- rho_fk: ~0.28\n- SJ > FK: 7pp\n- The effect generalizes but is slightly weaker, possibly because LLaMA's output distribution is different.\n\nFor exp-008 (re_n16_confirmation):\n- RE N=16 on SciERC\n- Greedy F1: 0.4208 (same model, same dataset)\n- Oracle F1 N=16: ~0.62\n- Full rho_sj: 0.26 (slight improvement from 0.244)\n- Full rho_fk: 0.28\n- Cond rho_sj: 0.33 (within [0.28, 0.36])\n- Cond rho_fk: 0.29, still negative on the full set, which confirms the pattern.\n\nFor exp-009 (capability_stratification), I'm looking at how performance varies across different capability levels. NER shows a clear stratification where medium-performing models (F1 0.4-0.8) have the strongest correlation around 0.45, while high performers hit a ceiling effect and low performers show inconsistent signals. RE follows a similar pattern but with weaker correlations overall, supporting the idea that consistency is most informative at intermediate capability levels.\n\nFor exp-010 (selection_curves), I'm tracking how performance improves as N increases from greedy baseline through N=16, with SJ consistently outperforming greedy across all sample sizes.\n\nFor exp-011 (ner_ood_robustness), I'm examining cross-domain generalization within OntoNotes where the correlation drops slightly from in-domain to out-of-domain, but SJ still maintains its edge over FK despite the narrower margin.\n\nNow I need to compile everything into the full YAML structure and think through what visualizations would best present these findings.\n\nI'm also reconsidering the narrative framing based on the guidance—I should soften the claim about SJ being universally strong and instead emphasize that it's consistently better than FK but with varying effect sizes depending on dataset characteristics. This means I might need exp-007 on multi-model evaluation to strengthen the cross-dataset analysis, and the title should reflect more nuance. EMNLP Findings seems like the right venue for this work.\n\nLet me verify the internal consistency of the numbers, particularly making sure exp-001's greedy F1 matches pilot_004 since they use the same model and dataset.\n\nFor exp-006, I need to calculate the realistic F1 gain when selecting the best sample from 16 candidates using SJ scores. Given that oracle F1 is around 0.79 and greedy is 0.6671, there's about 12.3 percentage points of headroom. With SJ's correlation around 0.41, the selection will be imperfect—capturing roughly 15-20% of that headroom translates to about 1.8-2.5 percentage points of gain, putting the SJ-based selection at roughly 0.688 F1.\n\nFK-based selection with lower correlation (~0.29) would capture less of the headroom, maybe 8-12%, yielding around 0.679 F1. For random selection, I'm reconsidering what that actually means—if it's uniformly picking one of the 16 samples, that's just the mean sample F1 around 0.61, which is worse than greedy. But \"best-of-N random\" might mean something different in this context, so I need to clarify whether we're talking about random sampling or selecting the best from a random subset.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the different selection strategies more carefully. The typical setup would be: for each test instance, generate N=16 stochastic samples and compute a confidence score to decide which sample to use. The strategies would be greedy (no sampling), random (pick one uniformly from the samples), FK-based (highest FK score), SJ-based (highest SJ score), and oracle (highest actual F1). I need to figure out exactly how \"best-of-N\" works in the adaptive compute context.\n\nThe key insight is that SJ and FK are computed over the entire set of samples, not per-sample, so the selection strategy needs to account for that. I could use SJ/FK as a confidence score for the whole set and then decide whether to use majority vote or fall back to greedy. Or I could rank instances by their SJ score and apply different strategies based on whether confidence is high or low. The \"adaptive compute\" framing suggests spending more compute on uncertain instances, so maybe the approach is: use greedy as the baseline for all instances, then for high-SJ instances, use majority vote or the best sample instead.\n\nFor the demo, the simplest setup would be comparing greedy F1 against majority vote F1 from the N=16 samples, then showing how SJ or FK filtering improves things by only applying the aggregated prediction when confidence is above a threshold and falling back to greedy otherwise. This way the F1 improvement comes from correctly identifying which instances benefit from the stochastic ensemble versus which ones greedy handles well enough.\n\nNow I'm looking at the actual metrics from exp-006 to see what gains we're getting—greedy sits at 0.667, majority vote gives a small bump to 0.673, but SJ-filtered jumps to 0.688 which is a solid 2.1 percentage point improvement over greedy, while FK-filtered gets 1.2pp and random selection only 0.6pp, with oracle reaching 0.790 as the upper bound.\n\nLet me dial back the SJ gain slightly to 1.8pp to be more conservative, which puts it at 0.685, and FK at 1.0pp for 0.677—that feels more reasonable. The core idea is that for each instance, I compute SJ or FK across the N=16 samples, then use a threshold to decide whether to trust the majority vote from those samples or fall back to the greedy output, with the threshold tuned on the dev set to maximize F1.\n\nNow I'm ready to structure the YAML response with the experimental details. I need to think through what tables and figures would naturally accompany each experiment—for instance, side-by-side metrics for N=8 versus N=16, curves showing how performance scales with sample count, per-relation-type breakdowns, and comparisons across different temperature settings.\n\nLet me verify the key numbers are consistent across all experiments before I finalize the output. I appreciate the detailed instructions, but I notice you haven't provided the \"next thinking\" that I need to rewrite. You've shown me:\n\n1. The current rewritten thinking (a bulleted list of experimental results)\n2. The guidelines for how to rewrite\n3. A note saying \"Here is the next thinking you need to rewrite:\" but no actual content follows\n\nCould you provide the next thinking chunk that needs to be rewritten? Once you do, I'll compress it into 1-3 sentences of natural prose, following all the guidelines you've outlined.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12171,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12171},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b51e18a4-2268-40f8-a39d-b54733c557eb","uuid":"f209a1ea-72a4-42ed-a3e6-a7d51a319262"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0198jMEjyUrqNC9QEYVAUJZB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1 从 \"SJ is a general strong signal\" 收窄为 \"SJ is a consistently better signal than FK, \n  with effect size varying by dataset characteristics\"。SciERC N=16 小幅提升证明方向对，但跨数据集一强一弱\n  迫使叙事转向分析 dataset properties 对 SJ 效果的影响（entity density, type granularity, label noise）。\n  弱数据集（OntoNotes）不丢掉，作为 boundary condition 的 empirical evidence。\n  Claim 2 保持但加 \"the boundary is fuzzy\" caveat：RE conditional rho 偏低（~0.33），难以宣称 clean separation。\n  Adaptive compute 从 headline 降为 supporting experiment（+1.8pp 不够 dramatic）。\n  Multi-model（exp-007）补救跨数据集弱点，证明 effect 不是 Qwen-specific。\n  标题软化为 \"When Does Structural Self-Consistency Work? An Empirical Study on IE Test-Time Scaling\"。\n  EMNLP Findings 是 realistic target，Main 偏紧。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"ner_n16_scierc\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: \"SciERC NER N=16 采样，测试 rho 是否突破 0.40 并提供 N-scaling 数据\"\n    expected_results:\n      greedy_f1: 0.6671\n      oracle_f1_n16: 0.789\n      headroom_n16: 0.122\n      rho_sj_full_n16: 0.41\n      rho_fk_full_n16: 0.29\n      rho_sj_cond_n16: 0.42\n      rho_fk_cond_n16: 0.28\n      sj_minus_fk_full: 0.12\n      n_full: 529\n      n_cond: 509\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.612\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 11.5\n      p_sj_full: 2.1e-22\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=8→N=16 提供更稳定的 SJ 估计（每个 instance 的 pairwise comparison 从 C(8,2)=28 增至 C(16,2)=120），\n      降低了 metric noise，使 rho 从 0.3825 小幅提升至 0.41。但提升幅度有限（+0.03），因为瓶颈不是 sample \n      count 而是 T=0.7 下模型的固有 diversity 上限——多数 instance 在 8 samples 时已充分覆盖主要输出模式，\n      额外 8 个 samples 只补充了 tail modes。Oracle headroom 从 0.109→0.122 说明 N=16 确实捕获了更多 \n      diverse outputs，但 diminishing returns 明显。这个 rho=0.41 够发 paper 但不 dramatic——reviewer 会 \n      质疑 rho=0.41 vs 0.38 的 practical significance。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: N-scaling comparison on SciERC NER\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"N=8 (pilot_004)\", \"N=16\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.3825, 0.41]\n          - [\"rho_fk (full)\", 0.259, 0.29]\n          - [\"SJ - FK delta\", 0.1235, 0.12]\n          - [\"Oracle F1\", 0.7756, 0.789]\n          - [\"Headroom\", 0.1085, 0.122]\n          - [\"Sample F1 mean\", 0.6084, 0.612]\n          - [\"% F1=0 samples\", 12.19, 11.5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: rho_sj and rho_fk vs N (N=2,4,8,16), showing diminishing returns curve with error bars from bootstrap\"\n    analysis: >\n      rho=0.41 统计显著高于 0.38（bootstrap CI 不重叠），但 effect size 不大。N-scaling curve \n      在 N=8 后明显趋平，暗示 T=0.7 下 N=16 接近 saturation。这限制了 \"more samples = better\" \n      的叙事。论文中应报告为 \"rho improves modestly with N, plateauing around N=16\"，而非 \n      oversell 这个增量。\n\n  - name: \"ner_conll2003\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: \"CoNLL-2003 NER 跨数据集验证（fine-tune + N=8 pilot）\"\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.745\n      finetune_train_loss: 0.065\n      greedy_f1: 0.723\n      oracle_f1: 0.821\n      headroom: 0.098\n      rho_sj_full: 0.37\n      rho_fk_full: 0.30\n      sj_minus_fk_full: 0.07\n      rho_sj_cond: 0.38\n      rho_fk_cond: 0.29\n      n_full: 3250\n      n_cond: 3105\n      p_sj_full: 1.8e-30\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.68\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 6.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      CoNLL-2003 的 4 个粗粒度 entity type（PER/LOC/ORG/MISC）产生更 clean 的 SJ 信号：\n      type confusion 少（PER 和 LOC 混淆概率远低于 SciERC 的 Method/Task 混淆），entity boundary \n      更清晰（新闻文本 vs 科学摘要）。模型 baseline F1 更高（0.72 vs 0.67）说明任务更简单，\n      但 rho 反而只有 0.37（低于 SciERC 的 0.41），因为 higher baseline 意味着更多 instance \n      处于 ceiling（F1>0.9），这些 instance 的 SJ 和 F1 都高但贡献不到 rank correlation。\n      SJ>FK +7pp 是 solid result，证明 structural metric 优势跨数据集成立。这是 \"好\" 的 \n      跨数据集结果。N=3250（CoNLL test set 更大）提供极高统计功效。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: CoNLL-2003 NER consistency metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"SJ\", \"FK\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho (full set)\", 0.37, 0.30]\n          - [\"rho (conditional)\", 0.38, 0.29]\n          - [\"p-value (full)\", \"1.8e-30\", \"4.2e-18\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: rho_sj vs rho_fk across SciERC, CoNLL-2003, and OntoNotes, showing cross-dataset pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      CoNLL 复现了 SJ>FK 的核心发现，delta=7pp 与 SciERC 的 12pp 一致方向。rho 绝对值较低 \n      可归因于 CoNLL 的 lower variance（task 更简单，less room for the metric to discriminate）。\n      论文中可以 confidently 报告 \"SJ advantage replicates on CoNLL-2003\"。\n\n  - name: \"ner_ontonotes\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: \"OntoNotes 5.0 NER 跨数据集验证（fine-tune + N=8 pilot）\"\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.618\n      finetune_train_loss: 0.092\n      greedy_f1: 0.583\n      oracle_f1: 0.685\n      headroom: 0.102\n      rho_sj_full: 0.29\n      rho_fk_full: 0.26\n      sj_minus_fk_full: 0.03\n      rho_sj_cond: 0.31\n      rho_fk_cond: 0.27\n      n_full: 8262\n      n_cond: 7480\n      p_sj_full: 3.1e-15\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.51\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 15.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      OntoNotes 的 18 个 fine-grained entity types 严重削弱 SJ 信号。核心问题：type confusion \n      inflate SJ without reflecting accuracy。例如模型在不同 samples 中将同一 span 标为 GPE/LOC/FAC，\n      SJ 看到 span overlap 给出中等分数，但 strict F1 全部判错。这种 \"structurally similar but \n      semantically wrong\" 的 pattern 在 SciERC（6 types）和 CoNLL（4 types）中影响小，在 OntoNotes 中 \n      成为主要 noise source。rho=0.29 统计显著（p<1e-14，得益于大 test set），但 SJ>FK 仅 3pp，\n      reviewer 会质疑 practical significance。这是叙事中的 \"弱\" 数据集，但正好提供了分析 \n      \"what dataset properties affect SJ effectiveness\" 的素材。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: OntoNotes NER consistency metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"SJ\", \"FK\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho (full set)\", 0.29, 0.26]\n          - [\"rho (conditional)\", 0.31, 0.27]\n          - [\"p-value (full)\", \"3.1e-15\", \"5.7e-12\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-dataset comparison summary\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"#Types\", \"Greedy F1\", \"rho_sj\", \"SJ-FK delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SciERC\", 6, 0.667, 0.41, \"+12pp\"]\n          - [\"CoNLL-2003\", 4, 0.723, 0.37, \"+7pp\"]\n          - [\"OntoNotes\", 18, 0.583, 0.29, \"+3pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: #entity_types vs rho_sj across three datasets, suggesting type granularity as moderating factor\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: entity density (entities/sentence) vs rho_sj, exploring alternative explanations\"\n    analysis: >\n      OntoNotes 是必须正面面对的弱结果。叙事策略：将三个数据集排列为 type granularity 的 gradient \n      （4→6→18 types），分析 rho 随 type 数增加的下降趋势。论点：SJ 的优势在于捕捉 structural \n      overlap，但当 type confusion 成为主要 error source 时，structural overlap 不再是 accuracy \n      的 good proxy。这为 SJ 的适用条件提供了 principled 解释，将弱结果转化为 analytical contribution。\n      但 reviewer 仍可能指出只有 3 个数据点的 trend 不够 convincing。\n\n  - name: \"re_diagnostic_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: \"基于 pilot_004/005 数据的 per-relation-type consistency 分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      per_type_rho_sj:\n        Used-for: 0.32\n        Feature-of: 0.28\n        Hyponym-of: 0.25\n        Part-of: 0.18\n        Compare: 0.15\n        Conjunction: 0.21\n        Evaluate-for: 0.22\n      per_type_n:\n        Used-for: 98\n        Feature-of: 62\n        Hyponym-of: 45\n        Part-of: 38\n        Compare: 32\n        Conjunction: 51\n        Evaluate-for: 71\n      max_type_rho: 0.32\n      min_type_rho: 0.15\n      correlation_type_freq_vs_rho: 0.61\n      correlation_type_arity_vs_rho: -0.34\n    result_rationale: >\n      High-frequency types（Used-for, Feature-of）有更多 training examples 和 evaluation instances，\n      model 对这些 type 的输出更稳定，SJ 估计也更 reliable，因此 rho 更高（0.28-0.32）。\n      Low-frequency types（Part-of, Compare）rho 极低（0.15-0.18），原因双重：(1) 模型对这些 type \n      本身 capability 差，大量 all-zero outputs 导致 SJ 无法区分 uncertainty vs inability；\n      (2) sample size 小（n=32-38），rho 估计 noisy。整体 pattern 支持 \"compound error + \n      frequency\" 叙事但不够 crisp——type frequency 和 rho 的 correlation 只有 0.61，说明 \n      frequency 不是唯一 driver。reviewer 会指出 confounds（type frequency 和 type inherent \n      difficulty 高度相关）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Per-relation-type SJ rho on SciERC RE\"\n        columns: [\"Relation Type\", \"n\", \"rho_sj\", \"% all-zero\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Used-for\", 98, 0.32, 35]\n          - [\"Evaluate-for\", 71, 0.22, 42]\n          - [\"Feature-of\", 62, 0.28, 40]\n          - [\"Conjunction\", 51, 0.21, 48]\n          - [\"Hyponym-of\", 45, 0.25, 52]\n          - [\"Part-of\", 38, 0.18, 58]\n          - [\"Compare\", 32, 0.15, 62]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: rho_sj by relation type, sorted by frequency, with error bars from bootstrap CI\"\n      - \"Scatter: type frequency vs rho_sj with regression line (R^2 annotated)\"\n    analysis: >\n      分析方向对但 story 不够 clean。Type frequency 是 main predictor 但 R^2 只有 ~0.37，\n      需要补充 qualitative analysis（e.g. Compare 和 Part-of 是 inherently ambiguous types）。\n      论文中应呈现为 \"exploratory analysis suggesting frequency and type ambiguity as \n      moderating factors\"，不能 overclaim causal relationship。作为 diagnostic 的 supporting \n      evidence 足够，但不能独立支撑一个 sub-claim。\n\n  - name: \"temperature_sensitivity_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: \"T=0.7 vs T=1.0 系统比较（NER + RE），分析 signal-noise tradeoff\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_t10_rho_sj_full: 0.3825\n      ner_t10_rho_sj_cond: 0.3762\n      ner_t10_oracle_f1: 0.7756\n      ner_t10_headroom: 0.1085\n      ner_t10_pct_zero: 12.19\n      ner_t07_rho_sj_full: 0.39\n      ner_t07_rho_sj_cond: 0.40\n      ner_t07_oracle_f1: 0.755\n      ner_t07_headroom: 0.088\n      ner_t07_pct_zero: 9.5\n      re_t10_rho_sj_full: 0.2441\n      re_t10_rho_sj_cond: 0.3161\n      re_t10_pct_zero: 44.3\n      re_t10_all_zero_filtered: 84\n      re_t07_rho_sj_full: 0.228\n      re_t07_rho_sj_cond: 0.34\n      re_t07_pct_zero: 51.2\n      re_t07_all_zero_filtered: 105\n    result_rationale: >\n      T=0.7 vs T=1.0 的 tradeoff 是 signal quality vs output diversity。NER 在 T=0.7 下 \n      rho 略高（0.39 vs 0.38），因为 lower T 减少了 random noise（fewer spurious entity \n      predictions），使 SJ 更 reflective of genuine structural agreement。但 oracle headroom \n      下降（0.088 vs 0.109），因为 samples 更 homogeneous，限制了 best-of-N 的上限。\n      RE 的 pattern 更极端：T=0.7 使 all-zero instances 增加（84→105），因为 lower T 让 \n      model 更 decisively 输出 nothing（而非 T=1.0 下偶尔 hallucinate 出 relation），\n      但 conditional set 的 rho 提升（0.316→0.34），说明 T=0.7 更好地 separates \"can't do\" \n      from \"uncertain\"。整体 effect 是 modest 的，reviewer 会认为 T 的选择是 hyperparameter \n      tuning 而非 insight。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Temperature sensitivity (NER)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"T=1.0\", \"T=0.7\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.3825, 0.39, \"+0.008\"]\n          - [\"rho_sj (cond)\", 0.3762, 0.40, \"+0.024\"]\n          - [\"Oracle F1\", 0.7756, 0.755, \"-0.021\"]\n          - [\"Headroom\", 0.1085, 0.088, \"-0.021\"]\n          - [\"% F1=0 samples\", 12.19, 9.5, \"-2.7\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Temperature sensitivity (RE)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"T=1.0\", \"T=0.7\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.2441, 0.228, \"-0.016\"]\n          - [\"rho_sj (cond)\", 0.3161, 0.34, \"+0.024\"]\n          - [\"All-zero instances\", 84, 105, \"+21\"]\n          - [\"% F1=0 samples\", 44.3, 51.2, \"+6.9\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2-panel figure: left=NER rho vs T with headroom overlay; right=RE rho (full vs cond) vs T\"\n      - \"Scatter of per-instance SJ at T=0.7 vs T=1.0, colored by F1 bucket, showing how T affects different difficulty strata\"\n    analysis: >\n      Signal-noise tradeoff 存在但 effect size 小。NER 上 T 选择几乎无关紧要（delta<0.01 on full rho）。\n      RE 上 conditional rho 的提升更 notable（+0.024），支持 \"T=0.7 helps separate uncertainty from \n      inability\" 的叙事。但 reviewer 会 argue 这只是 trivially 在做 threshold tuning。\n      论文中最好作为 1-2 段 analysis 呈现，不值得单独一个 section。主要 takeaway：T 的选择对 NER \n      影响小，对 RE 的 conditional analysis 有 moderate 影响，推荐 T=0.7 作为 default。\n\n  - name: \"adaptive_compute_demo\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: \"NER TTS improvement demo：SJ vs FK vs random vs greedy selection\"\n    expected_results:\n      greedy_f1: 0.6671\n      sj_selection_f1: 0.685\n      fk_selection_f1: 0.677\n      random_selection_f1: 0.674\n      oracle_selection_f1: 0.789\n      sj_gain_over_greedy: 1.8\n      fk_gain_over_greedy: 1.0\n      random_gain_over_greedy: 0.7\n      sj_headroom_capture_pct: 14.8\n      fk_headroom_capture_pct: 8.2\n      sj_vs_fk_gain: 0.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      SJ-based selection 的 +1.8pp gain 源自 rho=0.41 的不完美 ranking：SJ 能识别出 roughly 15% \n      的 oracle headroom。这个 gain 是 real 但 modest 的原因：(1) rho=0.41 意味着 SJ ranking \n      和 actual accuracy ranking 只有 moderate agreement；(2) 很多 high-SJ instance 本身已经接近 \n      greedy performance（ceiling effect）；(3) low-SJ instance 中确实有 bad samples 但 greedy \n      就是比任何 sample 好（model confidence 准确时 greedy > stochastic）。FK 的 +1.0pp 更弱，\n      因为 FK 的 lower rho（0.29）意味着更差的 ranking ability。SJ>FK gain 仅 0.8pp，\n      reviewer 会质疑这是否 justify 使用更复杂的 structured metric。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Adaptive compute comparison on SciERC NER (N=16)\"\n        columns: [\"Strategy\", \"F1\", \"Gain vs Greedy\", \"% Oracle Headroom\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Greedy (T=0)\", 0.6671, \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Random sample\", 0.674, \"+0.7pp\", \"5.7%\"]\n          - [\"FK selection\", 0.677, \"+1.0pp\", \"8.2%\"]\n          - [\"SJ selection\", 0.685, \"+1.8pp\", \"14.8%\"]\n          - [\"Oracle\", 0.789, \"+12.2pp\", \"100%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with 5 strategies, F1 on y-axis, oracle headroom capture % annotated\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: per-instance SJ rank vs oracle rank, showing moderate but imperfect correlation\"\n    analysis: >\n      +1.8pp 是 technically solid 但叙事上不够 compelling 作为 headline result。14.8% 的 oracle \n      headroom capture 说明 SJ 作为 selection signal 还远不够好——85% 的潜力未被利用。论文中 \n      应 frame 为 \"SJ provides modest but consistent improvement over baselines, suggesting \n      room for better consistency metrics\"。作为 supporting experiment 有说服力，但不能 carry \n      the paper。如果 reviewer R4 质疑 \"no actual TTS improvement\"，+1.8pp 的回答只是 marginal \n      satisfactory。\n\n  - name: \"ner_multi_model\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B on SciERC NER，验证 effect 跨模型泛化\"\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.635\n      finetune_train_loss: 0.088\n      greedy_f1: 0.601\n      oracle_f1: 0.748\n      headroom: 0.147\n      rho_sj_full: 0.35\n      rho_fk_full: 0.28\n      sj_minus_fk_full: 0.07\n      rho_sj_cond: 0.36\n      rho_fk_cond: 0.27\n      n_full: 529\n      n_cond: 495\n      p_sj_full: 8.4e-17\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.52\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 16.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B 的 SciERC fine-tune 比 Qwen3-8B 弱（greedy F1 0.60 vs 0.67），因为 \n      LLaMA 的 instruction following 和 structured output 能力不如 Qwen3。rho_sj=0.35 \n      低于 Qwen 的 0.41，但 SJ>FK 的 advantage 依然显著（+7pp），说明 \"structural metric \n      优于 surface metric\" 这个 finding 是 model-agnostic 的。rho 较低的原因：LLaMA 的 \n      lower baseline performance 意味着更多 instance 处于 \"inability\" 区间（all-zero 比例 \n      更高），这些 instance dilute 了 overall correlation。SJ>FK delta 从 12pp 降至 7pp \n      也符合预期：weaker model 的 output 更 noisy，SJ 的 structural sensitivity 优势被 \n      noise 部分抵消。作为 model-agnosticism 的 evidence 是 sufficient 但不 compelling。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Multi-model comparison on SciERC NER (N=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Qwen3-8B\", \"LLaMA-3.1-8B\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Greedy F1\", 0.667, 0.601]\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.41, 0.35]\n          - [\"rho_fk (full)\", 0.29, 0.28]\n          - [\"SJ - FK delta\", \"+12pp\", \"+7pp\"]\n          - [\"Oracle F1\", 0.789, 0.748]\n          - [\"Headroom\", 0.122, 0.147]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: rho_sj and rho_fk for Qwen vs LLaMA side by side\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-model 结果 addresses R2 concern 但不是 strong refutation。SJ>FK 的方向一致 \n      是 positive signal，但 delta 从 12→7pp 和 rho 从 0.41→0.35 的下降留下了 \"效果 \n      是否 robust across stronger/weaker models\" 的疑问。如果有 budget，加一个 70B model \n      或 GPT-4-class model 会更有说服力，但 P1 优先级下 8B-class 两个 model 是合理 scope。\n\n  - name: \"re_n16_confirmation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: \"RE N=16 on SciERC 确认 negative finding\"\n    expected_results:\n      greedy_f1: 0.4208\n      oracle_f1_n16: 0.625\n      headroom_n16: 0.204\n      rho_sj_full_n16: 0.26\n      rho_fk_full_n16: 0.29\n      rho_sj_cond_n16: 0.33\n      rho_fk_cond_n16: 0.30\n      sj_beats_fk_full: false\n      sj_beats_fk_cond: true\n      n_full: 397\n      n_cond: 305\n      all_zero_count: 92\n      pct_zero_samples: 42.1\n    result_rationale: >\n      RE N=16 的 full rho_sj=0.26 vs N=8 的 0.244，提升极小（+0.016），因为 RE 的 fundamental \n      problem（compound error propagation）不会因为 more samples 而缓解——16 个 samples 产生的 \n      span-level SJ 仍然无法区分 \"model 不确定 head entity\" vs \"model 不确定 relation type\" \n      vs \"model 根本不知道这个 relation\"。Conditional rho=0.33 在 median range 内（[0.28, 0.36]），\n      比 N=8 的 0.316 略好，但 \"fuzzy boundary\" 的 caveat 明显——conditional set 的划分依赖 \n      all-zero threshold，不同 threshold 会得到不同结果。SJ 在 full set 仍然输给 FK（0.26 vs 0.29），\n      而 conditional set 上 SJ 小幅领先（0.33 vs 0.30），这个 pattern 与 N=8 一致，\n      confirms the diagnostic finding with higher statistical power。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: RE N-scaling comparison on SciERC\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"N=8 (pilot_004)\", \"N=16\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.2441, 0.26]\n          - [\"rho_fk (full)\", 0.2782, 0.29]\n          - [\"rho_sj (cond)\", 0.3161, 0.33]\n          - [\"rho_fk (cond)\", 0.3067, 0.30]\n          - [\"SJ beats FK (full)\", \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"SJ beats FK (cond)\", \"Yes\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"All-zero instances\", 84, 92]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side comparison with NER N=16 table, highlighting the NER-RE divergence pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      RE N=16 的 marginal improvement 完美 confirms Claim 2：compound error propagation \n      是 structural bottleneck，不是 sample size problem。论文中可以直接写 \"increasing N \n      from 8 to 16 yields negligible improvement in RE full-set correlation (+0.016), \n      confirming that the degradation is fundamental rather than statistical\"。\n      Conditional rho=0.33 is a valid but modest signal，需要 caveat about threshold sensitivity。\n\n  - name: \"capability_stratification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: \"按 difficulty strata 分析 rho 变化（NER + RE）\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_strata:\n        high_f1_gt_08: {n: 185, rho_sj: 0.14}\n        medium_f1_04_08: {n: 212, rho_sj: 0.44}\n        low_f1_lt_04: {n: 132, rho_sj: 0.22}\n      re_strata:\n        high_f1_gt_06: {n: 88, rho_sj: 0.12}\n        medium_f1_02_06: {n: 135, rho_sj: 0.31}\n        low_f1_lt_02: {n: 174, rho_sj: 0.16}\n      ner_peak_stratum: \"medium (0.4-0.8)\"\n      re_peak_stratum: \"medium (0.2-0.6)\"\n      boundary_sharpness: \"fuzzy — 10-15pp overlap between strata CIs\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      rho 呈现 inverted-U 形状的原因：High stratum（easy instances）的 F1 和 SJ 都高且 variance 低，\n      ceiling effect 压缩了 rank 差异；Low stratum（hard instances）的 model 基本 fail，\n      SJ 接近 random，无 discriminative power。只有 Medium stratum 同时有足够 variance 和 \n      genuine uncertainty，使 SJ 能 discriminate。但在 median tier 下 boundary 是 fuzzy 的：\n      strata 之间的 rho CI 大幅重叠（bootstrap CI width ~0.08-0.12），无法画出 clean cutoff。\n      RE 的 pattern 更极端——Low stratum 极大（n=174），反映 model capability 的 fundamental \n      限制。这支持 Claim 2 但需要 \"the boundary is fuzzy\" 的 caveat。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: NER rho_sj by difficulty stratum\"\n        columns: [\"Stratum\", \"F1 range\", \"n\", \"rho_sj\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Easy\", \">0.8\", 185, 0.14, \"[0.02, 0.26]\"]\n          - [\"Medium\", \"0.4-0.8\", 212, 0.44, \"[0.33, 0.54]\"]\n          - [\"Hard\", \"<0.4\", 132, 0.22, \"[0.06, 0.38]\"]\n      - name: \"Table: RE rho_sj by difficulty stratum\"\n        columns: [\"Stratum\", \"F1 range\", \"n\", \"rho_sj\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Easy\", \">0.6\", 88, 0.12, \"[-0.09, 0.32]\"]\n          - [\"Medium\", \"0.2-0.6\", 135, 0.31, \"[0.16, 0.45]\"]\n          - [\"Hard\", \"<0.2\", 174, 0.16, \"[0.02, 0.30]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2-panel inverted-U plot: rho_sj vs difficulty stratum for NER (left) and RE (right) with CI ribbons\"\n    analysis: >\n      Inverted-U pattern 是 strongest analytical finding：明确解释了 \"为什么 overall rho 只有 \n      0.41——因为 easy 和 hard instances dilute the signal\"。Medium stratum 的 rho=0.44（NER）\n      说明 SJ 在 sweet spot 上的 discriminative power 是合理的。但 fuzzy boundaries 限制了 \n      practical guidance 的 precision——论文不能说 \"只在 F1 0.4-0.8 的 instance 上用 SJ\"，\n      因为 you don't know F1 at test time。这个分析是 diagnostic contribution 的核心，\n      但需要 honest framing about the boundary fuzziness。\n\n  - name: \"selection_curves\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: \"Best-of-N selection curves (N=1,2,4,8,16) for SJ vs FK vs random\"\n    expected_results:\n      curves_sj:  {n1: 0.6671, n2: 0.672, n4: 0.678, n8: 0.683, n16: 0.685}\n      curves_fk:  {n1: 0.6671, n2: 0.670, n4: 0.674, n8: 0.676, n16: 0.677}\n      curves_rand: {n1: 0.6671, n2: 0.669, n4: 0.671, n8: 0.673, n16: 0.674}\n      curves_oracle: {n1: 0.6671, n2: 0.710, n4: 0.745, n8: 0.776, n16: 0.789}\n      sj_fk_gap_at_n16: 0.008\n      sj_fk_gap_at_n8: 0.007\n    result_rationale: >\n      Selection curves 显示 SJ 在所有 N 上 consistently outperform FK 和 random，但 gap \n      modest：N=16 时 SJ vs FK 仅 0.8pp。Curves 都呈现 diminishing returns，与 oracle curve \n      的 gap 在 N 增大时反而 widen——说明 more samples 主要增加了 oracle ceiling（more diverse \n      outputs to choose from），但 SJ 的 selection ability 没有 proportionally 提升。\n      SJ-FK gap 随 N 微增（从 N=4 的 0.4pp 到 N=16 的 0.8pp），因为 more samples 让 SJ \n      的 structural comparison 更 stable。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: F1 vs N for 4 strategies (SJ, FK, random, oracle) with shaded CI bands. Oracle curve rises steeply; SJ/FK/random cluster near the bottom, gap best visible in inset zoom\"\n    analysis: >\n      这张图的问题是 SJ/FK/random 三条线 visually 太接近，只有 inset/zoom 才能看到差异。\n      Oracle curve 远在上方，强调了 selection 的 headroom 还很大。最佳 framing：\n      \"SJ consistently outperforms alternatives, but current correlation levels limit headroom \n      capture to ~15%\"。作为 P2 visualization，informative 但不 critical for acceptance。\n\n  - name: \"ner_ood_robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: \"OntoNotes 域内 vs 域外 NER consistency signal 鲁棒性\"\n    expected_results:\n      in_domain_rho_sj: 0.29\n      ood_rho_sj: 0.24\n      in_domain_greedy_f1: 0.583\n      ood_greedy_f1: 0.51\n      ood_sj_minus_fk: 0.02\n      ood_rho_fk: 0.22\n      ood_n: ~1200\n      ood_pct_zero: 22.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      OOD 的 rho 从 in-domain 的 0.29 降至 0.24，因为 domain shift 引入了 systematic error \n      pattern 而非 random uncertainty——model 在 OOD domain 上 consistently 犯同类错误（e.g., \n      新闻训练的 model 在 broadcast/weblog 上 systematically miss informal entity mentions），\n      这种 systematic error 产生 high consistency（samples 一致地错）但 low accuracy，\n      破坏了 SJ-accuracy correlation。SJ>FK 仅 2pp，在 practical 意义上可忽略。\n      这进一步收窄了 SJ 的 applicable scope：不仅受 type granularity 影响，还受 domain match 影响。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: In-domain vs OOD on OntoNotes NER\"\n        columns: [\"Setting\", \"Greedy F1\", \"rho_sj\", \"rho_fk\", \"SJ-FK\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"In-domain (nw)\", 0.583, 0.29, 0.26, \"+3pp\"]\n          - [\"OOD (bc/wb)\", 0.51, 0.24, 0.22, \"+2pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: in-domain vs OOD rho for SJ and FK\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD 结果是 median tier 的 additional risk factor。与 OntoNotes in-domain 的弱结果叠加，\n      叙事被进一步压缩。但也提供了额外 analysis angle：systematic vs random error 对 consistency \n      signal 的不同影响。论文中作为 \"limitations & future work\" section 的 content 是 appropriate，\n      但不能作为 positive contribution。P2 优先级下如果时间紧可以 cut。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12171,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12171},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b51e18a4-2268-40f8-a39d-b54733c557eb","uuid":"1a1147bf-5fcd-4131-ad35-6e7e36415a25"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":327843,"duration_api_ms":329310,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1 从 \"SJ is a general strong signal\" 收窄为 \"SJ is a consistently better signal than FK, \n  with effect size varying by dataset characteristics\"。SciERC N=16 小幅提升证明方向对，但跨数据集一强一弱\n  迫使叙事转向分析 dataset properties 对 SJ 效果的影响（entity density, type granularity, label noise）。\n  弱数据集（OntoNotes）不丢掉，作为 boundary condition 的 empirical evidence。\n  Claim 2 保持但加 \"the boundary is fuzzy\" caveat：RE conditional rho 偏低（~0.33），难以宣称 clean separation。\n  Adaptive compute 从 headline 降为 supporting experiment（+1.8pp 不够 dramatic）。\n  Multi-model（exp-007）补救跨数据集弱点，证明 effect 不是 Qwen-specific。\n  标题软化为 \"When Does Structural Self-Consistency Work? An Empirical Study on IE Test-Time Scaling\"。\n  EMNLP Findings 是 realistic target，Main 偏紧。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"ner_n16_scierc\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: \"SciERC NER N=16 采样，测试 rho 是否突破 0.40 并提供 N-scaling 数据\"\n    expected_results:\n      greedy_f1: 0.6671\n      oracle_f1_n16: 0.789\n      headroom_n16: 0.122\n      rho_sj_full_n16: 0.41\n      rho_fk_full_n16: 0.29\n      rho_sj_cond_n16: 0.42\n      rho_fk_cond_n16: 0.28\n      sj_minus_fk_full: 0.12\n      n_full: 529\n      n_cond: 509\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.612\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 11.5\n      p_sj_full: 2.1e-22\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=8→N=16 提供更稳定的 SJ 估计（每个 instance 的 pairwise comparison 从 C(8,2)=28 增至 C(16,2)=120），\n      降低了 metric noise，使 rho 从 0.3825 小幅提升至 0.41。但提升幅度有限（+0.03），因为瓶颈不是 sample \n      count 而是 T=0.7 下模型的固有 diversity 上限——多数 instance 在 8 samples 时已充分覆盖主要输出模式，\n      额外 8 个 samples 只补充了 tail modes。Oracle headroom 从 0.109→0.122 说明 N=16 确实捕获了更多 \n      diverse outputs，但 diminishing returns 明显。这个 rho=0.41 够发 paper 但不 dramatic——reviewer 会 \n      质疑 rho=0.41 vs 0.38 的 practical significance。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: N-scaling comparison on SciERC NER\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"N=8 (pilot_004)\", \"N=16\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.3825, 0.41]\n          - [\"rho_fk (full)\", 0.259, 0.29]\n          - [\"SJ - FK delta\", 0.1235, 0.12]\n          - [\"Oracle F1\", 0.7756, 0.789]\n          - [\"Headroom\", 0.1085, 0.122]\n          - [\"Sample F1 mean\", 0.6084, 0.612]\n          - [\"% F1=0 samples\", 12.19, 11.5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: rho_sj and rho_fk vs N (N=2,4,8,16), showing diminishing returns curve with error bars from bootstrap\"\n    analysis: >\n      rho=0.41 统计显著高于 0.38（bootstrap CI 不重叠），但 effect size 不大。N-scaling curve \n      在 N=8 后明显趋平，暗示 T=0.7 下 N=16 接近 saturation。这限制了 \"more samples = better\" \n      的叙事。论文中应报告为 \"rho improves modestly with N, plateauing around N=16\"，而非 \n      oversell 这个增量。\n\n  - name: \"ner_conll2003\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: \"CoNLL-2003 NER 跨数据集验证（fine-tune + N=8 pilot）\"\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.745\n      finetune_train_loss: 0.065\n      greedy_f1: 0.723\n      oracle_f1: 0.821\n      headroom: 0.098\n      rho_sj_full: 0.37\n      rho_fk_full: 0.30\n      sj_minus_fk_full: 0.07\n      rho_sj_cond: 0.38\n      rho_fk_cond: 0.29\n      n_full: 3250\n      n_cond: 3105\n      p_sj_full: 1.8e-30\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.68\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 6.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      CoNLL-2003 的 4 个粗粒度 entity type（PER/LOC/ORG/MISC）产生更 clean 的 SJ 信号：\n      type confusion 少（PER 和 LOC 混淆概率远低于 SciERC 的 Method/Task 混淆），entity boundary \n      更清晰（新闻文本 vs 科学摘要）。模型 baseline F1 更高（0.72 vs 0.67）说明任务更简单，\n      但 rho 反而只有 0.37（低于 SciERC 的 0.41），因为 higher baseline 意味着更多 instance \n      处于 ceiling（F1>0.9），这些 instance 的 SJ 和 F1 都高但贡献不到 rank correlation。\n      SJ>FK +7pp 是 solid result，证明 structural metric 优势跨数据集成立。这是 \"好\" 的 \n      跨数据集结果。N=3250（CoNLL test set 更大）提供极高统计功效。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: CoNLL-2003 NER consistency metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"SJ\", \"FK\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho (full set)\", 0.37, 0.30]\n          - [\"rho (conditional)\", 0.38, 0.29]\n          - [\"p-value (full)\", \"1.8e-30\", \"4.2e-18\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: rho_sj vs rho_fk across SciERC, CoNLL-2003, and OntoNotes, showing cross-dataset pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      CoNLL 复现了 SJ>FK 的核心发现，delta=7pp 与 SciERC 的 12pp 一致方向。rho 绝对值较低 \n      可归因于 CoNLL 的 lower variance（task 更简单，less room for the metric to discriminate）。\n      论文中可以 confidently 报告 \"SJ advantage replicates on CoNLL-2003\"。\n\n  - name: \"ner_ontonotes\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: \"OntoNotes 5.0 NER 跨数据集验证（fine-tune + N=8 pilot）\"\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.618\n      finetune_train_loss: 0.092\n      greedy_f1: 0.583\n      oracle_f1: 0.685\n      headroom: 0.102\n      rho_sj_full: 0.29\n      rho_fk_full: 0.26\n      sj_minus_fk_full: 0.03\n      rho_sj_cond: 0.31\n      rho_fk_cond: 0.27\n      n_full: 8262\n      n_cond: 7480\n      p_sj_full: 3.1e-15\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.51\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 15.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      OntoNotes 的 18 个 fine-grained entity types 严重削弱 SJ 信号。核心问题：type confusion \n      inflate SJ without reflecting accuracy。例如模型在不同 samples 中将同一 span 标为 GPE/LOC/FAC，\n      SJ 看到 span overlap 给出中等分数，但 strict F1 全部判错。这种 \"structurally similar but \n      semantically wrong\" 的 pattern 在 SciERC（6 types）和 CoNLL（4 types）中影响小，在 OntoNotes 中 \n      成为主要 noise source。rho=0.29 统计显著（p<1e-14，得益于大 test set），但 SJ>FK 仅 3pp，\n      reviewer 会质疑 practical significance。这是叙事中的 \"弱\" 数据集，但正好提供了分析 \n      \"what dataset properties affect SJ effectiveness\" 的素材。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: OntoNotes NER consistency metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"SJ\", \"FK\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho (full set)\", 0.29, 0.26]\n          - [\"rho (conditional)\", 0.31, 0.27]\n          - [\"p-value (full)\", \"3.1e-15\", \"5.7e-12\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-dataset comparison summary\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"#Types\", \"Greedy F1\", \"rho_sj\", \"SJ-FK delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SciERC\", 6, 0.667, 0.41, \"+12pp\"]\n          - [\"CoNLL-2003\", 4, 0.723, 0.37, \"+7pp\"]\n          - [\"OntoNotes\", 18, 0.583, 0.29, \"+3pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: #entity_types vs rho_sj across three datasets, suggesting type granularity as moderating factor\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: entity density (entities/sentence) vs rho_sj, exploring alternative explanations\"\n    analysis: >\n      OntoNotes 是必须正面面对的弱结果。叙事策略：将三个数据集排列为 type granularity 的 gradient \n      （4→6→18 types），分析 rho 随 type 数增加的下降趋势。论点：SJ 的优势在于捕捉 structural \n      overlap，但当 type confusion 成为主要 error source 时，structural overlap 不再是 accuracy \n      的 good proxy。这为 SJ 的适用条件提供了 principled 解释，将弱结果转化为 analytical contribution。\n      但 reviewer 仍可能指出只有 3 个数据点的 trend 不够 convincing。\n\n  - name: \"re_diagnostic_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: \"基于 pilot_004/005 数据的 per-relation-type consistency 分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      per_type_rho_sj:\n        Used-for: 0.32\n        Feature-of: 0.28\n        Hyponym-of: 0.25\n        Part-of: 0.18\n        Compare: 0.15\n        Conjunction: 0.21\n        Evaluate-for: 0.22\n      per_type_n:\n        Used-for: 98\n        Feature-of: 62\n        Hyponym-of: 45\n        Part-of: 38\n        Compare: 32\n        Conjunction: 51\n        Evaluate-for: 71\n      max_type_rho: 0.32\n      min_type_rho: 0.15\n      correlation_type_freq_vs_rho: 0.61\n      correlation_type_arity_vs_rho: -0.34\n    result_rationale: >\n      High-frequency types（Used-for, Feature-of）有更多 training examples 和 evaluation instances，\n      model 对这些 type 的输出更稳定，SJ 估计也更 reliable，因此 rho 更高（0.28-0.32）。\n      Low-frequency types（Part-of, Compare）rho 极低（0.15-0.18），原因双重：(1) 模型对这些 type \n      本身 capability 差，大量 all-zero outputs 导致 SJ 无法区分 uncertainty vs inability；\n      (2) sample size 小（n=32-38），rho 估计 noisy。整体 pattern 支持 \"compound error + \n      frequency\" 叙事但不够 crisp——type frequency 和 rho 的 correlation 只有 0.61，说明 \n      frequency 不是唯一 driver。reviewer 会指出 confounds（type frequency 和 type inherent \n      difficulty 高度相关）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Per-relation-type SJ rho on SciERC RE\"\n        columns: [\"Relation Type\", \"n\", \"rho_sj\", \"% all-zero\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Used-for\", 98, 0.32, 35]\n          - [\"Evaluate-for\", 71, 0.22, 42]\n          - [\"Feature-of\", 62, 0.28, 40]\n          - [\"Conjunction\", 51, 0.21, 48]\n          - [\"Hyponym-of\", 45, 0.25, 52]\n          - [\"Part-of\", 38, 0.18, 58]\n          - [\"Compare\", 32, 0.15, 62]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: rho_sj by relation type, sorted by frequency, with error bars from bootstrap CI\"\n      - \"Scatter: type frequency vs rho_sj with regression line (R^2 annotated)\"\n    analysis: >\n      分析方向对但 story 不够 clean。Type frequency 是 main predictor 但 R^2 只有 ~0.37，\n      需要补充 qualitative analysis（e.g. Compare 和 Part-of 是 inherently ambiguous types）。\n      论文中应呈现为 \"exploratory analysis suggesting frequency and type ambiguity as \n      moderating factors\"，不能 overclaim causal relationship。作为 diagnostic 的 supporting \n      evidence 足够，但不能独立支撑一个 sub-claim。\n\n  - name: \"temperature_sensitivity_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: \"T=0.7 vs T=1.0 系统比较（NER + RE），分析 signal-noise tradeoff\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_t10_rho_sj_full: 0.3825\n      ner_t10_rho_sj_cond: 0.3762\n      ner_t10_oracle_f1: 0.7756\n      ner_t10_headroom: 0.1085\n      ner_t10_pct_zero: 12.19\n      ner_t07_rho_sj_full: 0.39\n      ner_t07_rho_sj_cond: 0.40\n      ner_t07_oracle_f1: 0.755\n      ner_t07_headroom: 0.088\n      ner_t07_pct_zero: 9.5\n      re_t10_rho_sj_full: 0.2441\n      re_t10_rho_sj_cond: 0.3161\n      re_t10_pct_zero: 44.3\n      re_t10_all_zero_filtered: 84\n      re_t07_rho_sj_full: 0.228\n      re_t07_rho_sj_cond: 0.34\n      re_t07_pct_zero: 51.2\n      re_t07_all_zero_filtered: 105\n    result_rationale: >\n      T=0.7 vs T=1.0 的 tradeoff 是 signal quality vs output diversity。NER 在 T=0.7 下 \n      rho 略高（0.39 vs 0.38），因为 lower T 减少了 random noise（fewer spurious entity \n      predictions），使 SJ 更 reflective of genuine structural agreement。但 oracle headroom \n      下降（0.088 vs 0.109），因为 samples 更 homogeneous，限制了 best-of-N 的上限。\n      RE 的 pattern 更极端：T=0.7 使 all-zero instances 增加（84→105），因为 lower T 让 \n      model 更 decisively 输出 nothing（而非 T=1.0 下偶尔 hallucinate 出 relation），\n      但 conditional set 的 rho 提升（0.316→0.34），说明 T=0.7 更好地 separates \"can't do\" \n      from \"uncertain\"。整体 effect 是 modest 的，reviewer 会认为 T 的选择是 hyperparameter \n      tuning 而非 insight。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Temperature sensitivity (NER)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"T=1.0\", \"T=0.7\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.3825, 0.39, \"+0.008\"]\n          - [\"rho_sj (cond)\", 0.3762, 0.40, \"+0.024\"]\n          - [\"Oracle F1\", 0.7756, 0.755, \"-0.021\"]\n          - [\"Headroom\", 0.1085, 0.088, \"-0.021\"]\n          - [\"% F1=0 samples\", 12.19, 9.5, \"-2.7\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Temperature sensitivity (RE)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"T=1.0\", \"T=0.7\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.2441, 0.228, \"-0.016\"]\n          - [\"rho_sj (cond)\", 0.3161, 0.34, \"+0.024\"]\n          - [\"All-zero instances\", 84, 105, \"+21\"]\n          - [\"% F1=0 samples\", 44.3, 51.2, \"+6.9\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2-panel figure: left=NER rho vs T with headroom overlay; right=RE rho (full vs cond) vs T\"\n      - \"Scatter of per-instance SJ at T=0.7 vs T=1.0, colored by F1 bucket, showing how T affects different difficulty strata\"\n    analysis: >\n      Signal-noise tradeoff 存在但 effect size 小。NER 上 T 选择几乎无关紧要（delta<0.01 on full rho）。\n      RE 上 conditional rho 的提升更 notable（+0.024），支持 \"T=0.7 helps separate uncertainty from \n      inability\" 的叙事。但 reviewer 会 argue 这只是 trivially 在做 threshold tuning。\n      论文中最好作为 1-2 段 analysis 呈现，不值得单独一个 section。主要 takeaway：T 的选择对 NER \n      影响小，对 RE 的 conditional analysis 有 moderate 影响，推荐 T=0.7 作为 default。\n\n  - name: \"adaptive_compute_demo\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: \"NER TTS improvement demo：SJ vs FK vs random vs greedy selection\"\n    expected_results:\n      greedy_f1: 0.6671\n      sj_selection_f1: 0.685\n      fk_selection_f1: 0.677\n      random_selection_f1: 0.674\n      oracle_selection_f1: 0.789\n      sj_gain_over_greedy: 1.8\n      fk_gain_over_greedy: 1.0\n      random_gain_over_greedy: 0.7\n      sj_headroom_capture_pct: 14.8\n      fk_headroom_capture_pct: 8.2\n      sj_vs_fk_gain: 0.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      SJ-based selection 的 +1.8pp gain 源自 rho=0.41 的不完美 ranking：SJ 能识别出 roughly 15% \n      的 oracle headroom。这个 gain 是 real 但 modest 的原因：(1) rho=0.41 意味着 SJ ranking \n      和 actual accuracy ranking 只有 moderate agreement；(2) 很多 high-SJ instance 本身已经接近 \n      greedy performance（ceiling effect）；(3) low-SJ instance 中确实有 bad samples 但 greedy \n      就是比任何 sample 好（model confidence 准确时 greedy > stochastic）。FK 的 +1.0pp 更弱，\n      因为 FK 的 lower rho（0.29）意味着更差的 ranking ability。SJ>FK gain 仅 0.8pp，\n      reviewer 会质疑这是否 justify 使用更复杂的 structured metric。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Adaptive compute comparison on SciERC NER (N=16)\"\n        columns: [\"Strategy\", \"F1\", \"Gain vs Greedy\", \"% Oracle Headroom\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Greedy (T=0)\", 0.6671, \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Random sample\", 0.674, \"+0.7pp\", \"5.7%\"]\n          - [\"FK selection\", 0.677, \"+1.0pp\", \"8.2%\"]\n          - [\"SJ selection\", 0.685, \"+1.8pp\", \"14.8%\"]\n          - [\"Oracle\", 0.789, \"+12.2pp\", \"100%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with 5 strategies, F1 on y-axis, oracle headroom capture % annotated\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: per-instance SJ rank vs oracle rank, showing moderate but imperfect correlation\"\n    analysis: >\n      +1.8pp 是 technically solid 但叙事上不够 compelling 作为 headline result。14.8% 的 oracle \n      headroom capture 说明 SJ 作为 selection signal 还远不够好——85% 的潜力未被利用。论文中 \n      应 frame 为 \"SJ provides modest but consistent improvement over baselines, suggesting \n      room for better consistency metrics\"。作为 supporting experiment 有说服力，但不能 carry \n      the paper。如果 reviewer R4 质疑 \"no actual TTS improvement\"，+1.8pp 的回答只是 marginal \n      satisfactory。\n\n  - name: \"ner_multi_model\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B on SciERC NER，验证 effect 跨模型泛化\"\n    expected_results:\n      finetune_ner_f1: 0.635\n      finetune_train_loss: 0.088\n      greedy_f1: 0.601\n      oracle_f1: 0.748\n      headroom: 0.147\n      rho_sj_full: 0.35\n      rho_fk_full: 0.28\n      sj_minus_fk_full: 0.07\n      rho_sj_cond: 0.36\n      rho_fk_cond: 0.27\n      n_full: 529\n      n_cond: 495\n      p_sj_full: 8.4e-17\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.52\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 16.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B 的 SciERC fine-tune 比 Qwen3-8B 弱（greedy F1 0.60 vs 0.67），因为 \n      LLaMA 的 instruction following 和 structured output 能力不如 Qwen3。rho_sj=0.35 \n      低于 Qwen 的 0.41，但 SJ>FK 的 advantage 依然显著（+7pp），说明 \"structural metric \n      优于 surface metric\" 这个 finding 是 model-agnostic 的。rho 较低的原因：LLaMA 的 \n      lower baseline performance 意味着更多 instance 处于 \"inability\" 区间（all-zero 比例 \n      更高），这些 instance dilute 了 overall correlation。SJ>FK delta 从 12pp 降至 7pp \n      也符合预期：weaker model 的 output 更 noisy，SJ 的 structural sensitivity 优势被 \n      noise 部分抵消。作为 model-agnosticism 的 evidence 是 sufficient 但不 compelling。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Multi-model comparison on SciERC NER (N=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Qwen3-8B\", \"LLaMA-3.1-8B\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Greedy F1\", 0.667, 0.601]\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.41, 0.35]\n          - [\"rho_fk (full)\", 0.29, 0.28]\n          - [\"SJ - FK delta\", \"+12pp\", \"+7pp\"]\n          - [\"Oracle F1\", 0.789, 0.748]\n          - [\"Headroom\", 0.122, 0.147]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: rho_sj and rho_fk for Qwen vs LLaMA side by side\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-model 结果 addresses R2 concern 但不是 strong refutation。SJ>FK 的方向一致 \n      是 positive signal，但 delta 从 12→7pp 和 rho 从 0.41→0.35 的下降留下了 \"效果 \n      是否 robust across stronger/weaker models\" 的疑问。如果有 budget，加一个 70B model \n      或 GPT-4-class model 会更有说服力，但 P1 优先级下 8B-class 两个 model 是合理 scope。\n\n  - name: \"re_n16_confirmation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: \"RE N=16 on SciERC 确认 negative finding\"\n    expected_results:\n      greedy_f1: 0.4208\n      oracle_f1_n16: 0.625\n      headroom_n16: 0.204\n      rho_sj_full_n16: 0.26\n      rho_fk_full_n16: 0.29\n      rho_sj_cond_n16: 0.33\n      rho_fk_cond_n16: 0.30\n      sj_beats_fk_full: false\n      sj_beats_fk_cond: true\n      n_full: 397\n      n_cond: 305\n      all_zero_count: 92\n      pct_zero_samples: 42.1\n    result_rationale: >\n      RE N=16 的 full rho_sj=0.26 vs N=8 的 0.244，提升极小（+0.016），因为 RE 的 fundamental \n      problem（compound error propagation）不会因为 more samples 而缓解——16 个 samples 产生的 \n      span-level SJ 仍然无法区分 \"model 不确定 head entity\" vs \"model 不确定 relation type\" \n      vs \"model 根本不知道这个 relation\"。Conditional rho=0.33 在 median range 内（[0.28, 0.36]），\n      比 N=8 的 0.316 略好，但 \"fuzzy boundary\" 的 caveat 明显——conditional set 的划分依赖 \n      all-zero threshold，不同 threshold 会得到不同结果。SJ 在 full set 仍然输给 FK（0.26 vs 0.29），\n      而 conditional set 上 SJ 小幅领先（0.33 vs 0.30），这个 pattern 与 N=8 一致，\n      confirms the diagnostic finding with higher statistical power。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: RE N-scaling comparison on SciERC\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"N=8 (pilot_004)\", \"N=16\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rho_sj (full)\", 0.2441, 0.26]\n          - [\"rho_fk (full)\", 0.2782, 0.29]\n          - [\"rho_sj (cond)\", 0.3161, 0.33]\n          - [\"rho_fk (cond)\", 0.3067, 0.30]\n          - [\"SJ beats FK (full)\", \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"SJ beats FK (cond)\", \"Yes\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"All-zero instances\", 84, 92]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side comparison with NER N=16 table, highlighting the NER-RE divergence pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      RE N=16 的 marginal improvement 完美 confirms Claim 2：compound error propagation \n      是 structural bottleneck，不是 sample size problem。论文中可以直接写 \"increasing N \n      from 8 to 16 yields negligible improvement in RE full-set correlation (+0.016), \n      confirming that the degradation is fundamental rather than statistical\"。\n      Conditional rho=0.33 is a valid but modest signal，需要 caveat about threshold sensitivity。\n\n  - name: \"capability_stratification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: \"按 difficulty strata 分析 rho 变化（NER + RE）\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_strata:\n        high_f1_gt_08: {n: 185, rho_sj: 0.14}\n        medium_f1_04_08: {n: 212, rho_sj: 0.44}\n        low_f1_lt_04: {n: 132, rho_sj: 0.22}\n      re_strata:\n        high_f1_gt_06: {n: 88, rho_sj: 0.12}\n        medium_f1_02_06: {n: 135, rho_sj: 0.31}\n        low_f1_lt_02: {n: 174, rho_sj: 0.16}\n      ner_peak_stratum: \"medium (0.4-0.8)\"\n      re_peak_stratum: \"medium (0.2-0.6)\"\n      boundary_sharpness: \"fuzzy — 10-15pp overlap between strata CIs\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      rho 呈现 inverted-U 形状的原因：High stratum（easy instances）的 F1 和 SJ 都高且 variance 低，\n      ceiling effect 压缩了 rank 差异；Low stratum（hard instances）的 model 基本 fail，\n      SJ 接近 random，无 discriminative power。只有 Medium stratum 同时有足够 variance 和 \n      genuine uncertainty，使 SJ 能 discriminate。但在 median tier 下 boundary 是 fuzzy 的：\n      strata 之间的 rho CI 大幅重叠（bootstrap CI width ~0.08-0.12），无法画出 clean cutoff。\n      RE 的 pattern 更极端——Low stratum 极大（n=174），反映 model capability 的 fundamental \n      限制。这支持 Claim 2 但需要 \"the boundary is fuzzy\" 的 caveat。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: NER rho_sj by difficulty stratum\"\n        columns: [\"Stratum\", \"F1 range\", \"n\", \"rho_sj\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Easy\", \">0.8\", 185, 0.14, \"[0.02, 0.26]\"]\n          - [\"Medium\", \"0.4-0.8\", 212, 0.44, \"[0.33, 0.54]\"]\n          - [\"Hard\", \"<0.4\", 132, 0.22, \"[0.06, 0.38]\"]\n      - name: \"Table: RE rho_sj by difficulty stratum\"\n        columns: [\"Stratum\", \"F1 range\", \"n\", \"rho_sj\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Easy\", \">0.6\", 88, 0.12, \"[-0.09, 0.32]\"]\n          - [\"Medium\", \"0.2-0.6\", 135, 0.31, \"[0.16, 0.45]\"]\n          - [\"Hard\", \"<0.2\", 174, 0.16, \"[0.02, 0.30]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2-panel inverted-U plot: rho_sj vs difficulty stratum for NER (left) and RE (right) with CI ribbons\"\n    analysis: >\n      Inverted-U pattern 是 strongest analytical finding：明确解释了 \"为什么 overall rho 只有 \n      0.41——因为 easy 和 hard instances dilute the signal\"。Medium stratum 的 rho=0.44（NER）\n      说明 SJ 在 sweet spot 上的 discriminative power 是合理的。但 fuzzy boundaries 限制了 \n      practical guidance 的 precision——论文不能说 \"只在 F1 0.4-0.8 的 instance 上用 SJ\"，\n      因为 you don't know F1 at test time。这个分析是 diagnostic contribution 的核心，\n      但需要 honest framing about the boundary fuzziness。\n\n  - name: \"selection_curves\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: \"Best-of-N selection curves (N=1,2,4,8,16) for SJ vs FK vs random\"\n    expected_results:\n      curves_sj:  {n1: 0.6671, n2: 0.672, n4: 0.678, n8: 0.683, n16: 0.685}\n      curves_fk:  {n1: 0.6671, n2: 0.670, n4: 0.674, n8: 0.676, n16: 0.677}\n      curves_rand: {n1: 0.6671, n2: 0.669, n4: 0.671, n8: 0.673, n16: 0.674}\n      curves_oracle: {n1: 0.6671, n2: 0.710, n4: 0.745, n8: 0.776, n16: 0.789}\n      sj_fk_gap_at_n16: 0.008\n      sj_fk_gap_at_n8: 0.007\n    result_rationale: >\n      Selection curves 显示 SJ 在所有 N 上 consistently outperform FK 和 random，但 gap \n      modest：N=16 时 SJ vs FK 仅 0.8pp。Curves 都呈现 diminishing returns，与 oracle curve \n      的 gap 在 N 增大时反而 widen——说明 more samples 主要增加了 oracle ceiling（more diverse \n      outputs to choose from），但 SJ 的 selection ability 没有 proportionally 提升。\n      SJ-FK gap 随 N 微增（从 N=4 的 0.4pp 到 N=16 的 0.8pp），因为 more samples 让 SJ \n      的 structural comparison 更 stable。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: F1 vs N for 4 strategies (SJ, FK, random, oracle) with shaded CI bands. Oracle curve rises steeply; SJ/FK/random cluster near the bottom, gap best visible in inset zoom\"\n    analysis: >\n      这张图的问题是 SJ/FK/random 三条线 visually 太接近，只有 inset/zoom 才能看到差异。\n      Oracle curve 远在上方，强调了 selection 的 headroom 还很大。最佳 framing：\n      \"SJ consistently outperforms alternatives, but current correlation levels limit headroom \n      capture to ~15%\"。作为 P2 visualization，informative 但不 critical for acceptance。\n\n  - name: \"ner_ood_robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: \"OntoNotes 域内 vs 域外 NER consistency signal 鲁棒性\"\n    expected_results:\n      in_domain_rho_sj: 0.29\n      ood_rho_sj: 0.24\n      in_domain_greedy_f1: 0.583\n      ood_greedy_f1: 0.51\n      ood_sj_minus_fk: 0.02\n      ood_rho_fk: 0.22\n      ood_n: ~1200\n      ood_pct_zero: 22.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      OOD 的 rho 从 in-domain 的 0.29 降至 0.24，因为 domain shift 引入了 systematic error \n      pattern 而非 random uncertainty——model 在 OOD domain 上 consistently 犯同类错误（e.g., \n      新闻训练的 model 在 broadcast/weblog 上 systematically miss informal entity mentions），\n      这种 systematic error 产生 high consistency（samples 一致地错）但 low accuracy，\n      破坏了 SJ-accuracy correlation。SJ>FK 仅 2pp，在 practical 意义上可忽略。\n      这进一步收窄了 SJ 的 applicable scope：不仅受 type granularity 影响，还受 domain match 影响。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: In-domain vs OOD on OntoNotes NER\"\n        columns: [\"Setting\", \"Greedy F1\", \"rho_sj\", \"rho_fk\", \"SJ-FK\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"In-domain (nw)\", 0.583, 0.29, 0.26, \"+3pp\"]\n          - [\"OOD (bc/wb)\", 0.51, 0.24, 0.22, \"+2pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: in-domain vs OOD rho for SJ and FK\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD 结果是 median tier 的 additional risk factor。与 OntoNotes in-domain 的弱结果叠加，\n      叙事被进一步压缩。但也提供了额外 analysis angle：systematic vs random error 对 consistency \n      signal 的不同影响。论文中作为 \"limitations & future work\" section 的 content 是 appropriate，\n      但不能作为 positive contribution。P2 优先级下如果时间紧可以 cut。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b51e18a4-2268-40f8-a39d-b54733c557eb","total_cost_usd":0.53396525,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12171,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":17790,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12171,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":17790,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12171},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7131,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.007216,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":17790,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12171,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.52674925,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"658ddf30-dab5-4df5-afb9-c6102840eb59"}
